# React Native and Expo require a hoisted node_modules layout.
#
# pnpm's default strict linking nests every package under
# .pnpm/<name>@<version>/node_modules/<name> and exposes only declared
# dependencies. React Native's tooling (Metro, jest-expo, the autolinking
# scripts) resolves a long tail of transitive packages it never declares —
# @react-native/assets-registry is the first of many — and simply fails to find
# them. This is the layout Expo documents for pnpm workspaces.
#
# It costs pnpm's strictness repo-wide, which is a real trade: an undeclared
# dependency will now resolve instead of erroring. The alternative is listing
# React Native's internal graph by hand and re-listing it on every SDK bump.
node-linker=hoisted
